--TEST--
`exit` stops the program where it stands: no `catch` sees it and no `finally` above it runs — docs/adr/README.md § Decisions taken at project start
--FILE--
<?nvs
// covers: lang:programs/ending-a-program
// PHP's `exit` is not an unwind. It is neither catchable nor observable by a
// `finally`, in the frame that runs it or in any frame above — which is what
// makes it a fourth ABI status rather than a `throw` with a nicer name.
// Checked against PHP's own output rather than assumed.
class Deep {
    public static function inner(): void {
        string $held = "held";
        echo $held, "\n";
        exit(0);
    }
}
echo "before\n";
try {
    Deep::inner();
} catch (Throwable $e) {
    echo "caught\n";
} finally {
    echo "finally\n";
}
echo "after\n";
--EXPECT--
before
held
